      <Graphics centerX="1600.0" centerY="891.463134765625" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">|FRAME: Ceramides &quot;A ceramide&quot;| is a lipid molecule that is composed of the sphingoid base |FRAME: SPHINGOSINE| and |FRAME: Fatty-Acids|. |FRAME: CPD3DJ-82 &quot;A dihydroceramide&quot;| is composed of the sphingoid base |FRAME: CPD-13612| (where the double bond in the |FRAME: SPHINGOSINE| tail has been reduced) and a fatty acid. |FRAME: CPD3DJ-82 &quot;Dihydroceramides&quot;| are also known as &quot;plant ceramide (I)&quot;.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPD3DJ-82" />
